\par When correcting \'93letter by letter\'94, the programme compares the user\rquote s answer to the closest possible answer and tries to identify any missing, extra or wrong characters.
\par The algorithm used to do this comparison is quite complex: when a difference is found between the two expressions one text is shifted in relation to the other until 
a significant number of coincidences is found, so then it may go on comparing with the maximum amount of guesses. Every movement of an expression in relation to the other is called a }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 step}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . The amount of characters placed before and after the character that caused the mistake compared at every step is the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 exploration field}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
. It is advisable not to change the default values for these fields unless the correction \'93letter by letter\'94 is unable to identify the most common mistakes the students make.
