ume that the file you are referring to is in the same location as the activity calling it. You may also indicate absolute MS-DOS paths, with a special characteristic if the drive name is }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 CDR}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 : you must look for the files in the first CD-ROM drive in the system. For instance, the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{car.bmp\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  means it must display the }{
\i\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 car.bmp}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  file that is in the same directory as the activity. The expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{c:\\graphics\\car.bmp\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 means the file is in the }{\i\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 c:\\graphics }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 directory, and the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{cdr: \\graphics\\vehicles\\car.bmp\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 indicates the file is in the }{\i\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \\graphics\\vehicles}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  directory in the first CD-ROM drive in the computer. If there is not a CD-ROM drive or you don\rquote 
t have the correct disk inserted in it, an error will occur. You will find a more detailed explanation of these concepts under }{\uldb\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 File Organisation}{\v\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 HELP_ORGARX}{
