This icon will be displayed in the cells that only include an imported }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 .WAV}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  recorded sound file. These files can be created with the \lquote Sound Recorder\rquote  programme.
\par Besides the name of the WAV file, you may also indicate the initial and final positions of the fragment you want to listen to when activating the cell. These positions must be indicated in milliseconds and must be written after the words }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 from}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  and/or }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 to}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . For instance, with the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{dict.wav from 5000 to 8000\}}
{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  you will listen to a fragment of the dict.wav file extending between seconds 5 and 8.
\par If you omit one of the two parameters, the programme will play the fragment from the beginning or until the end. For example, }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{dict.wav from 9000\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 will play the sound file from second 9 (until the end) and }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{dict.wav to 3000\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  will play only the first three seconds.
