This icon will be displayed in those cells where the user may record his or her own voice with a microphone connected to the sound card. Clic allows you to record up to 10 different sounds in each activity, identified by the code }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 rec0}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 , }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 rec1}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 , }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 rec2}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 ... up to }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 rec9}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . Each one of these codes refers to a \'93virtual tape\'94 that Clic stores in its memory. After the code for each soun
d to be recorded, you may write a number to indicate the time limit of the recording, expressed in seconds. If you don\rquote t specify a different value, the system will use its default, which is 5 seconds.
\par For instance, a cell with the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{rec2 8\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  will 
allow the user to record his voice for 8 seconds. This sound will be saved in virtual tape number 2. During the recording, a microphone will be displayed at the mouse pointer.
\par Sound recording has been specially designed as an asset for language activities, to allow comparison between correct sound patterns (that can be shown in cells referring to WAV files) and the user\rquote 
s pronunciation. You can listen to recorded sounds by means of the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{recX play\} }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 code, described below, but you cannot record them on the disk.
\par \cell }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \trowd \trgaph70\trleft-70\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrnone \clbrdrl
