\par This is the icon displayed in cells where you can listen to the contents of the virtual tapes recorded as explained above. To listen to each one of the virtual tapes you must write its code followed by the word }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 play}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . For example, with the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{rec2 play\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  you would listen to the contents of virtual tape number two.
\par At the beginning of the activity all the virtual tapes are empty. If the user tries to listen to a sound that has not yet been recorded, an error message will occur. The }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{recX play\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 cells should only be used in combination with }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{recX\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  cells with the same code.
\par \cell }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \trowd \trgaph70\trleft-70\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrnone \clbrdrl
