\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 This is the icon shown in cells with an imported .}{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 MID}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  music file. You can create these files with any sequencer or music editor, like MusicTime, Encore, Finale...
\par As with WAV digital sound files, you may also specify here the fragment to be played with the words }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 from}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  and }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 to}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
. In this case, however, you don\rquote t use milliseconds as a unit but the number of sixteenth notes counting from the beginning of the melody. For example, for a song written in 3/4 time, the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{
vals.mid from 64 to 128\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  would only play the 3}{\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 rd}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  and 4}{\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 th}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 bars of the score.
\par \cell }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \trowd \trgaph70\trleft-70\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrnone \clbrdrl
