\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\cs16\lang1024\langfe1024\super\noproof\langnp2057 #}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\langnp2057  HELP_GRAFTX_CD}}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc icocd.bmp\}\cell 
This icon is displayed in cells that only contain a reference to a CD-Audio, which will be played on activation. To refer to a fragment in a music compact disc (or CD-Audio) you use the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{track:minute:second\} }{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 format. For instance, the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{02:00:15\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  indicates that the CD must begin playing at 15\'94 after the beginning of the second track.
\par Optionally, you may use the word }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 to}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  indicate when to stop playing. For example, the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{02:00:15 to 02:00:20\}}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  indicates you will listen to 5 seconds in the second track of the CD beginning from second 15.
\par \cell }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \trowd \trgaph70\trleft-70\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrnone \clbrdrl
