\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 #{\footnote \pard\plain \s15\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 
\f1\fs20\lang1027\langfe3082\cgrid\langnp1027\langfenp3082 {\cs16\lang1024\langfe1024\super\noproof\langnp2057 #}{\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof\langnp2057  HELP_GRAFTX_AVI}}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc icomci.bmp\}\cell 
This icon is displayed in cells that only import other types of multimedia resources, such as }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 .AVI}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  digital video files or }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 .FLI }{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 animations.
\par When playing digital video files the image will be aligned in the top left corner of the cell that contains them. To control the exact position and the size of the video window you may also specify two additional instructions:
\par 
\par }\pard \ql \li214\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin214 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 The expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{stretch\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 indicates that the video image has to be stretched or compressed to fit the cell.
\par 
\par The expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{free\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  indicates that the video window must be in the centre of the screen with its original size.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
\par For instance, a cell with the text }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{horse.avi\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  will display the }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 horse.avi}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 video sequence in its original size and aligned in the top left corner of the cell containing it. If the expression was }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{horse.avi\}\{stretch\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  it would fit the cell, and if it was }{
\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{horse.avi\}\{free\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  it would be in the centre of the screen.
\par Another way to adjust the position of the video window is to include within the main expression the text }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 pos}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 followed by three numeric parameters: horizontal offset, vertical offset and a third figure to indicate where to measure the offset from. This last figure must be a }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 0}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 if the offset takes place within the cell, a }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 1}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  if it is within the game window and a }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 2}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 if the offset is measured from the top left corner of the Clic's main window. For example, the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{horse.avi pos 15 20 2\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  will di
splay the video 15 points to the right and 20 points to the bottom, measured from Clic\rquote s main window top left corner. The expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{horse.avi pos 10 10 0\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
 would move the video 10 points in each direction within the cell from which you called it.
\par You can also indicate the length of the fragment to be played for digital video files by using the words }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 from}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  and }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 to}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . The lengths are indicated in milliseconds, just as in digital sound files.
\par \cell }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \trowd \trgaph70\trleft-70\trftsWidth1\trpaddl70\trpaddr70\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrnone \clbrdrl
