\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\intbl\hyphpar0\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{bmc icoexe.bmp\}}{\cs16\lang2057\langfe3082\super\langnp2057 \cell }{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 
You can also call up other programmes that can be run from Clic, when this icon will be displayed (unless an alternative graphic content is indicated). For example, the expression }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{calc.exe\}}{
\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057  will run Windows calculator when you click on the cell.
\par The names of the applicable files may be followed by parameters, for example }{\b\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 \{pbrush.exe drawing.bmp\}}{\lang2057\langfe3082\langnp2057 . This will activate PaintBrush with the image "drawing.bmp".
\par Clic is not responsible for closing the external programmes that have been opened by using these instructions in the cells. This function should be used with care, to avoid filling the screen with overlapping windows.
